Relevant columns and their potential usage  
• `population_by_country.country_code`: join key to health dataset  
• `population_by_country.year_2017`, `population_by_country.year_2018`: total population in 2017 & 2018 – used to compute % change ((y18‑y17)/y17).  
• `health_nutrition_population.country_code`: join key to population table  
• `health_nutrition_population.indicator_name` / `indicator_code`: identify “Current health expenditure per capita (PPP, current international $)” series.  
• `health_nutrition_population.value`: expenditure value for a given year – used to compute % change.  
• `health_nutrition_population.year`: pick 2017 vs 2018 rows.  

Typical filter / join conditions  
• `WHERE year IN (2017,2018)`  
• `WHERE indicator_code = 'SH.XPD.CHEX.PP.CD'`   -- (to be confirmed with discovery queries)  
• `population_by_country.year_2017 IS NOT NULL AND population_by_country.year_2018 IS NOT NULL`  
• `% change > 0.01`  

Below are ten exploration queries (LIMIT 20) that go from simple inspection to the final answer.  
Each is preceded by a brief description.

```sql
-- 1. Description: Find indicator names containing the key words “current health expenditure” and “per capita” and “PPP”.
SELECT DISTINCT indicator_name, indicator_code
FROM `bigquery-public-data.world_bank_health_population.health_nutrition_population`
WHERE LOWER(indicator_name) LIKE '%current health expenditure%'
  AND LOWER(indicator_name) LIKE '%per capita%'
  AND LOWER(indicator_name) LIKE '%ppp%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Description: Display 2018 observations for the candidate indicator codes we just discovered.
SELECT country_code, value, year, indicator_code
FROM `bigquery-public-data.world_bank_health_population.health_nutrition_population`
WHERE indicator_code = 'SH.XPD.CHEX.PP.CD'
  AND year = 2018
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Description: Inspect 2017 observations for the same indicator to be sure both years exist.
SELECT country_code, value, year
FROM `bigquery-public-data.world_bank_health_population.health_nutrition_population`
WHERE indicator_code = 'SH.XPD.CHEX.PP.CD'
  AND year = 2017
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Description: Preview population figures for 2017 & 2018 for a few countries.
SELECT country_code, country, year_2017, year_2018
FROM `bigquery-public-data.world_bank_global_population.population_by_country`
WHERE year_2017 IS NOT NULL
  AND year_2018 IS NOT NULL
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Description: Compute 2017‑2018 % growth in total population for sample countries (>1% flag).
SELECT country_code,
       SAFE_DIVIDE(year_2018 - year_2017, year_2017) AS pop_growth_frac
FROM `bigquery-public-data.world_bank_global_population.population_by_country`
WHERE year_2017 IS NOT NULL AND year_2018 IS NOT NULL
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Description: Compute 2017‑2018 % growth in per‑capita health expenditure (PPP) for sample countries.
WITH chex AS (
  SELECT country_code,
         MAX(CASE WHEN year = 2017 THEN value END) AS v2017,
         MAX(CASE WHEN year = 2018 THEN value END) AS v2018
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.world_bank_health_population.health_nutrition_population`
  WHERE indicator_code = 'SH.XPD.CHEX.PP.CD'
    AND year IN (2017,2018)
  GROUP BY country_code )
SELECT country_code,
       SAFE_DIVIDE(v2018 - v2017, v2017) AS chex_growth_frac
FROM chex
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Description: List countries whose population grew >1% from 2017 to 2018.
SELECT country_code
FROM `bigquery-public-data.world_bank_global_population.population_by_country`
WHERE year_2017 IS NOT NULL AND year_2018 IS NOT NULL
  AND SAFE_DIVIDE(year_2018 - year_2017, year_2017) > 0.01
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8. Description: List countries whose per‑capita health expenditure (PPP) grew >1% from 2017 to 2018.
WITH chex AS (
  SELECT country_code,
         MAX(CASE WHEN year = 2017 THEN value END) AS v2017,
         MAX(CASE WHEN year = 2018 THEN value END) AS v2018
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.world_bank_health_population.health_nutrition_population`
  WHERE indicator_code = 'SH.XPD.CHEX.PP.CD'
    AND year IN (2017,2018)
  GROUP BY country_code )
SELECT country_code
FROM chex
WHERE v2017 IS NOT NULL AND v2018 IS NOT NULL
  AND SAFE_DIVIDE(v2018 - v2017, v2017) > 0.01
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9. Description: Join previous two result sets to find overlap (both population & health‑spending grew >1%).
WITH pop AS (
  SELECT country_code
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.world_bank_global_population.population_by_country`
  WHERE year_2017 IS NOT NULL AND year_2018 IS NOT NULL
    AND SAFE_DIVIDE(year_2018 - year_2017, year_2017) > 0.01 ),
chex AS (
  SELECT country_code
  FROM (
    SELECT country_code,
           MAX(CASE WHEN year = 2017 THEN value END) AS v2017,
           MAX(CASE WHEN year = 2018 THEN value END) AS v2018
    FROM `bigquery-public-data.world_bank_health_population.health_nutrition_population`
    WHERE indicator_code = 'SH.XPD.CHEX.PP.CD'
      AND year IN (2017,2018)
    GROUP BY country_code )
  WHERE v2017 IS NOT NULL AND v2018 IS NOT NULL
    AND SAFE_DIVIDE(v2018 - v2017, v2017) > 0.01 )
SELECT p.country_code
FROM pop p
JOIN chex USING (country_code)
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--10. Description: Final query – count countries where BOTH metrics rose >1% from 2017 to 2018.
WITH pop AS (
  SELECT country_code
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.world_bank_global_population.population_by_country`
  WHERE year_2017 IS NOT NULL AND year_2018 IS NOT NULL
    AND SAFE_DIVIDE(year_2018 - year_2017, year_2017) > 0.01 ),
chex AS (
  SELECT country_code
  FROM (
    SELECT country_code,
           MAX(CASE WHEN year = 2017 THEN value END) AS v2017,
           MAX(CASE WHEN year = 2018 THEN value END) AS v2018
    FROM `bigquery-public-data.world_bank_health_population.health_nutrition_population`
    WHERE indicator_code = 'SH.XPD.CHEX.PP.CD'
      AND year IN (2017,2018)
    GROUP BY country_code )
  WHERE v2017 IS NOT NULL AND v2018 IS NOT NULL
    AND SAFE_DIVIDE(v2018 - v2017, v2017) > 0.01 )
SELECT COUNT(*) AS countries_with_both_growth_gt_1pct
FROM pop
JOIN chex USING (country_code);
```

