Table full name: bigquery-public-data.world_bank_wdi.series_summary
Column name: series_code Type: STRING Description: A number or a sequence of related statistical units arranged or occurring in temporal spatial or other order or succession. WDI carries mostly time series.
Column name: topic Type: STRING Description: The matter dealt with in the context discourse or subject related to the series.
Column name: indicator_name Type: STRING Description: Given name of a series.
Column name: short_definition Type: STRING Description: Short statement of the exact meaning of a series.
Column name: long_definition Type: STRING Description: Extended statement of the exact meaning of a series.
Column name: unit_of_measure Type: STRING Description: A quantity used as a standard of measurement. Example: Units of time are second minute hour day week month year and decade.
Column name: periodicity Type: STRING Description: Applies to series recurring at regular intervals. Most of the time this term denotes that interval of recurrence.
Column name: base_period Type: STRING Description: Base period is the period of time for which data is used as the base of an index number or other ratio have been collected. This period is frequently one of a year but it may be as short as one day or as long as the average of a group of years.
Column name: other_notes Type: STRING Description: A brief record of facts topics or thoughts written down and used to contextualize the series definition values and other characteristics.
Column name: aggregation_method Type: STRING Description: Aggregation methods are types of calculations used to group attribute values into a metric for each dimension value. For example for each region one may retrieve the total value of country entries (the sum of the series value for countries belonging to the region).
Column name: limitations_and_exceptions Type: STRING Description: A limiting rule or circumstance that applies to usage of the series such as the scope of the survey collecting the data or missing years and countries.  It should also note when data are imputed or estimated
Column name: notes_from_original_source Type: STRING Description: A brief record of facts topics or thoughts written down and used to contextualize the series definition values and other characteristics.
Column name: general_comments Type: STRING Description: Other notes regarding the series which do not appear in Development relevance or Limitations or exceptions
Column name: source Type: STRING Description: A place person or organization from which the series comes or can be obtained.
Column name: statistical_concept_and_methodology Type: STRING Description: The abstract idea general statistical notions or a system of methods used to generate the series.
Column name: development_relevance Type: STRING Description: The relevance of a series refers to how the indicator’s data may be used to monitor particular aspects of development goals and programs for example the Sustainable Development Goals. The indicator may conclusively measure progress towards a particular objective or may act as a proxy or interpretation of a development aim.
Column name: related_source_links Type: STRING Description: Internet address of related source page tool or knowledge base.
Column name: other_web_links Type: STRING Description: Internet addresses of related pages tools or knowledge bases.
Column name: related_indicators Type: STRING Description: In general indicator that are of interest and related to the specific series.
Column name: license_type Type: STRING Description: Explains the rights conferred and restrictions imposed by the owner to the users of a series
